      equipment: 'Domino set, score sheet or scoreboard.',
      dealing: "Tiles are 'washed' (shuffled) face down. Players draw their hand; remaining tiles are the 'Boneyard'.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Leading**: Any tile can be led. 2. **Matching**: Subsequent tiles must match the pips of an open end. 3. **Doubles**: Placed crosswise. They count as the sum of their pips until matched on both sides. 4. **The Spinner**: The first double played is the 'Spinner'. Once matched on its sides, tiles can be played off its ends, creating 4 open ends. 5. **Scoring**: After playing a tile, sum all open ends. If the total is a multiple of 5 (5, 10, 15, 20, etc.), the player immediately scores that many points. 6. **Boneyard**: If you cannot play, you must draw from the boneyard until you can. 7. **Dominoing**: The hand ends when a player uses their last tile. They score the remaining pips in their opponents' hands (rounded to the nearest 5).",
